package tk.darrow.tribalpower.guide;

import java.util.List;

/** Generated by tools/generate_guide.py. */
public final class GuidePages {
    private GuidePages() {}
    public static List<String> allPages() {
        return List.of(
            "SPIRIT CODEX\n\nThe old sky was nine tribes agreeing. Continents hung from living thread. Then the agreements failed, and what did not fall is the dirt under your feet.\n\nShamanic technomancy begins with a rhythm. Raise a camp that answers you: living power, elemental workshops, woven equipment and paths between worlds.\n\nHow:\n1. Craft a Spirit Codex (or take the one in your starter kit) and open it.\n2. Read First camp, then raise a Drumheart before you raise a factory.\n3. Sneak-use this book on any Tribal block if it sits silent \u2014 it will say why.\n4. Spoilers stay veiled until you choose Reveal, or until a Tribe Mark or tablet unlocks that page.",
            "THE WORLD THAT WAS\n\nBefore the void had a name, the sky was a floor. Nine Strands \u2014 Soil, Stone, Sprout, Claw, Spark, Clock, Swarm, Sigil, Spindle \u2014 were pulled taut by nine tribes. Continents hung from that lattice the way fruit hangs from a well-kept vine. Weather ran along it. Rain knew where to fall. Nothing dropped that was not meant to.\n\nRoads were sung into the thread and walked. Crops rooted into Strand as much as soil. Drums under one pad were heard as Pulse under another. The Loom was not a god and it was not a machine. It was nine agreements kept at once. When the tribes pulled together, the horizon stayed put. That is the whole of the old physics.\n\nFrom that pull came this craft: Pulse, lattice, seal, and the road into the March. The engines are still out there. Orphaned, humming, sacred. Treat them like an inheritance, not a scrap pile.",
            "WHEN THE AGREEMENTS FAILED\n\nSomething severed the Loom. This Codex does not know what. Neither did the tribes, by the end. One moment the sky was a floor. The next, the agreements failed in the same breath.\n\nThe Pad-keepers felt it first \u2014 hearths went cold while the sky still looked whole. Then the Rootbinders' living anchors held for a season, and that season is why anything is still up here. Guardians snapped in their arenas. Songs kept playing with nobody to hear them. Gate-paths stayed open into nowhere.\n\nThe Cut was not a war. It was a knot coming undone. Continents fell in the space of a drum-roll. What did not fall is a pad of earth the Strands still remember. You are standing on leftovers that learned how to be a floor.",
            "WHAT MENDING MEANS\n\nYou are not putting continents back. You are teaching nine voices to agree again, one camp at a time.\n\nA chalk link is a promise. A seated catalyst is a conversation restarted. A tablet rite is asking politely, smaller than the old world asked. A Strand token at a Tension Post is the same promise in another dialect.\n\nThe March kept the halls, the drums, the tablets. Read every tablet. Strike the Silent Drum when you are ready. Tell the camps we are sorry it took so long. The world does not snap back. It learns to hold.",
            "CONTINENTS OF THREAD\n\nA continent was a pad that had forgotten it was a pad. Fields ran because Soil ran with them. Rivers kept manners because Sprout taught water where to sit. Cities did not float. They hung, and hanging felt like standing.\n\nRoads were sung, not cut. Pulse under one hearth was heard as Pulse under the next. Night was an appointment the Seal-carvers kept. Storms were a Drumheart argument walked back before dawn.\n\nYou can still see the habit in the aurora. It is the sky trying to remember a schedule.",
            "NINE ARGUMENTS\n\nNo tribe could hold the sky alone. Soil without Stone is warmth with nowhere to stand. Spark without Clock is a beat with no song. Sigil without Spindle is a promise with no road home.\n\nThe old world was not peace. It was maintenance. Eight pulls became eight arguments. The cloth tore along the Loom-stitchers' seam, and then the rest went like a rope through a hand.\n\nThe Cut was not a war. It was nine jobs left undone in the same breath.",
            "THE MARCH AS REST\n\nThe March is where the thread frayed thinnest and the fallen ground came to rest. Halls lie sunk to the lintel. Camps keep time with no one at the drum. Crystal grows where the Loom's tension still pools.\n\nWalk it with a full Pulse cell and a steady hand. Ancestor Halls kept the tablets. Drum Circles kept the last beat. The Unsung is a keeper who went hollow waiting to be struck.\n\nEverything here still answers a beat. That is not haunting. That is a world that never learned how to quit.",
            "HOLDING IS THE WORK\n\nMending is not a private miracle. Seat a Strand and your pad notices. Seat nine and the cut above your pad closes. Other Clowders still have theirs to do; the Fray over the Dock is the public clock.\n\nRead every tablet. Strike the Silent Drum when you are ready. Offer at hearths. Ask politely, smaller than the old world asked.\n\nIf the Fray has gone to lit thread, the sky has learned to hold. If it has not, someone else still has work. Help them.",
            "FIRST CAMP\n\nRaise a drum before you raise a factory.\n\nHow:\n1. Craft a Bone Chime, a Spirit Shard and a Drumheart.\n2. Place the Drumheart. Strike it empty-handed, about a breath apart.\n3. Craft a Pulse Cell and use it on the drum to carry Pulse with you.\n4. JEI shows every recipe. Every system also works without another mod installed.",
            "SPIRIT PULSE\n\nPulse is the beat the old sky ran on. It comes from rhythm, landscape and harmony \u2014 not from coal.\n\nHow:\n1. Keep a generator within 8 blocks of the machine that needs it: Drumheart, Ley Collector, Pulse Resonator, or a tribe voice-craft.\n2. Machines draw from generators first, then from totem buffers a Conductor has filled.\n3. Use a Pulse Cell on a generator to carry Pulse with you for tools, rites and travel.\n4. A lever on a generator pauses it. Stored Pulse stays.\n5. Sneak-use the Spirit Codex on a silent machine to hear how much Pulse is in range.",
            "DRUMHEART\n\nThe drum is not loud. The drum is steady.\n\nHow:\n1. Place a Drumheart.\n2. Strike empty-handed, about one second apart, for 24 Pulse. Offbeat hits yield 10.\n3. Redstone pays the same tempo: a rising edge 17 to 23 ticks after the last beat is 24, anything else 10, nothing closer than 8 ticks.\n4. A one-second Heartbeat plate makes 24 a second; a spam clock makes 10.\n5. Use a Pulse Cell on it to carry the beat away.",
            "LEY COLLECTOR\n\nThe land still sings if you give it sky \u2014 and a grove, not a puddle.\n\nHow:\n1. Place the Ley Collector under open sky. It listens in an 8-block radius, the same as the lattice.\n2. Night, rain and storm, water, living plants, totem voices, a Tribe Hearth, nearby animals, a full moon and The March each add. A roofed hole stays at the base trickle.\n3. A strong pad (about half the cap) keeps nearby totems answered. The land remembers the camp so the factory does not go quiet.\n4. A redstone signal pauses generation. Rank it in Echo Attune, Bind, then Manifest to hum harder.\n5. Sneak-use a Ley Lens on it to print the exact factor breakdown. Hold the lens to paint the ground in a 17-by-17.",
            "KEEPING\n\nThe drum is not loud. The drum is steady. A clock can hold Pulse. It cannot hold a conversation.\n\nHow:\n1. A totem you use stays answered. A totem you ignore goes dim, then quiet.\n2. Quiet pauses new work. It does not dump the queue. Strike the totem or use a Bone Chime to wake it.\n3. A Heartbeat plate still feeds the drum. Stand in camp, run the matching station, keep Kin at a hearth, or site a strong Ley Collector if you want the voice to stay answered.\n4. A roofed hole forgets you faster. Open sky, water and greenery remember longer.\n5. Sneak-use the Codex on a silent totem. It will say whether it is hungry or merely unpowered.",
            "PULSE RESONATOR\n\nThe Resonator makes Pulse from harmony. It is not a furnace. Coal and wood do nothing.\n\nHow:\n1. Place the Pulse Resonator.\n2. Right-click it with an Echo catalyst. Start with an Echo Shard (Echo Shatter plus an Earth totem, using stone \u2014 cobble will not make shards).\n3. Place at least two different Resonance Totems within 8 blocks. Earth and Fire is enough.\n4. When it lights, it is working. The crystal stays seated; it is not burned. Sneak with an empty hand to take it back.\n5. Click empty-handed to read stored Pulse, gain per second, and how many voices it hears. Sneak-use the Spirit Codex on it if it sits silent.\n\nA lever on the Resonator pauses it. A heap of totems counts at most five voices; six voices need the Voice Ring (totems at radius 3).",
            "HARMONIC RANKS\n\nA catalyst is a reusable crystal you seat in the Resonator. Stronger crystals make more Pulse. None of them burn away.\n\nHow:\n1. Rank 1 \u2014 Echo Shard: shatter stone, deepslate or March stone in Echo Shatter with an Earth totem.\n2. Rank 2 \u2014 Attuned Echo: cook shards in Echo Attune with a Fire totem.\n3. Rank 3 \u2014 Bound Echo: cook attuned echoes in Echo Bind with a Water totem.\n4. Rank 4 \u2014 Resonant Core: cook Manifested Ingots in Echo Manifest with a Spirit totem.\n5. Seat the crystal. Each second the Resonator makes (2 times distinct voices) plus (2 times rank). Two voices and a shard is 6 Pulse a second. Six voices in a Voice Ring and a Core is 20.\n\nKinship Totems add extra tribe voices. Sneak empty-handed to lift the crystal. Redstone pauses generation.",
            "CARRY THE BEAT\n\nA cell is a drum you can put in a pocket.\n\nHow:\n1. Craft a Pulse Cell. Use it on a Drumheart or Resonator to charge it.\n2. Ordinary cells hold 200 Pulse. Greater Cells hold 1,200.\n3. Carry charged cells for spells, Spiritgear, charms, travel and tablet rites.\n4. Use a cell on a Gate Drum or keystone to pay travel costs.\n5. A Pulse Gauge pointed at a cell-holding machine reads how full the beat is.",
            "SIX VOICES\n\nEarth shatters. Fire attunes. Water binds. Spirit manifests. Air lends motion. Loom unweaves.\n\nHow:\n1. Craft the Resonance Totem of the voice you need.\n2. Place it within 8 blocks of the station. Missing voices pause work safely \u2014 nothing is spent.\n3. Earth for Shatter and the Stone Font. Fire for Attune and the Ember Kiln. Water for Bind. Spirit for Manifest. Air for motion and Song. Loom for Unweave and Far Gates.\n4. Kinship Totems count as extra tribe voices, not as a seventh element.\n5. Sneak-use the Codex on a paused station: it names the missing voice.",
            "CHALK AND CONDUCTOR\n\nThe Conductor does not make Pulse. It moves Pulse you already have, along chalk-linked totems.\n\nHow:\n1. Place two or more Resonance Totems.\n2. Right-click the first with Ritual Chalk, then the second (they must be within 16 blocks). You should see \"Lattice link sealed\".\n3. Place a Lattice Conductor within 8 blocks of those totems.\n4. Place a Drumheart, Ley Collector or Pulse Resonator within 8 blocks of the Conductor.\n5. Every second it pulls up to 10 Pulse from those generators and pushes it into the linked totems. Ranked conductors pull more. Song Benches that need help are filled first.\n6. Right-click the Conductor for a 25-Pulse burst and a status line.\n7. Every two seconds, if the lattice holds Pulse, it moves Echo items between Song Benches and nearby Ancestral Caches.\n\nA lever on the Conductor pauses it. \"No network\" means the totems are not chalk-linked. \"No Pulse\" means bring a generator closer. Ley Binding can also join distant totems as if they stood side by side.",
            "ECHO WORKSHOPS\n\nThe Echo stations process real batches. Ember Kiln is the sixth station \u2014 Fire attunement, vanilla smelting paid in Pulse.\n\nHow:\n1. Place the station. Matching Resonance Totem within 8.\n2. Open it. The IO pad sets each face to Input, Output, Both or Closed. Stations start Input on five faces and Output below.\n3. Sit a Shatter on a Kiln: grit walks down with no hopper and no relay. Beside them, set the touching faces to Output into Input.\n4. Hoppers and pipes still honour those faces. Relays are for distance.\n5. Full output pauses work. A lever pauses insert and work.\n\nFeed slot 0; take from slots 1-8. Pulse draw is doubled from 3.2: a hand Drumheart still runs Stone Font cobble, not these stations.",
            "SHATTER\n\nEarth turns stone into Echo Shards. Cobble does not sing: Echo Shatter hammers cobble to gravel, gravel to sand, then sand to Ex Deorum dust when that mod is loaded, or clay when it is not. Shards want stone, deepslate, or March stone.\n\nHow:\n1. Place Echo Shatter. Earth totem within 8.\n2. Feed from above or the sides. Sit it on an Ember Kiln (or a hopper) for output \u2014 matching Output into Input needs no pipe.\n3. Stone in, shards out (16 Pulse/s before the pack multiplier).\n4. Cobble in, gravel out (4 Pulse/s) \u2014 the hammer chain. Sand becomes dust with Ex Deorum, clay without it.\n5. Metals: raw item or silk-touched ore to grit, then grit to ingot in a furnace or Ember Kiln. Gems: silk-touched ore straight to the gem at twice the ore drop. The gem is never an input. Modded ores light up from common tags.",
            "ATTUNE AND BIND\n\nFire teaches a shard to remember heat. Water teaches it to stay.\n\nHow:\n1. Place Echo Attune with a Fire totem within 8. Feed Echo Shards. Take Attuned Echoes.\n2. Place Echo Bind with a Water totem within 8. Feed Attuned Echoes. Take Bound Echoes.\n3. Bind also turns wool into Spiritweave and dirt into clay.\n4. Sit Attune on Bind, Output into Input, and the chain walks without a hopper.\n5. JEI lists time and Pulse. A lever pauses either station.",
            "MANIFEST\n\nSpirit turns Bound Echoes into Manifested Ingots, then ingots into Resonant Cores.\n\nHow:\n1. Place Echo Manifest. Spirit totem within 8.\n2. Feed Bound Echoes. Take Manifested Ingots.\n3. Feed Manifested Ingots. Take Resonant Cores.\n4. Cores unlock Greater Cells, Spiritgear, long-distance automation and gate keystones.\n5. Sit Bind on Manifest, Output into Input, and the chain walks without a hopper.\n\nJEI lists time and Pulse. A lever pauses the station.",
            "SONG BENCH\n\nThe original single-item workshop remains. Dedicated Echo stations are better for sustained batches.\n\nHow:\n1. Place a Song Bench. Matching totem within 8.\n2. Insert one Echo-stage ingredient.\n3. Click empty-handed to sing. Sneak-click to take the item back.\n4. A Conductor on the lattice fills a hungry bench first.\n5. Rank it in Echo Attune, Bind, then Manifest: the song shortens, Pulse per tick rises, Pulse per craft stays about even.",
            "ANCESTRAL CACHE\n\nA local 54-slot inventory for camp supplies.\n\nHow:\n1. Place it beside or under a station.\n2. Open it. The IO pad sets each face to Input, Output, Both or Closed; sneak-empty-hand on a face does the same.\n3. Set the touching faces to Output into Input and the cache feeds or drains the station with no hopper and no relay. Both-into-Both does nothing, so stacks cannot ping-pong.\n4. Hoppers and pipes still honour those faces. Relays are for distance.\n5. A lever locks access and automation. A comparator reads how full it is.",
            "DEEP CACHE\n\nA personal 54-slot vault shared between every Deep Cache you place.\n\nHow:\n1. Place a Deep Cache.\n2. Visiting The March attunes you; otherwise opening costs 5 Pulse.\n3. A Wayfarer Satchel opens the same personal vault.\n4. Sneak-use the satchel to switch between your vault and a shared camp vault.\n5. A lever locks the block. The vault itself is not emptied by a pause.",
            "SPIRIT CISTERN\n\nStores 16 buckets of one fluid.\n\nHow:\n1. Place the cistern. Right-click with a bucket to fill or empty it.\n2. Standard fluid pipes and the Tide Pump both work.\n3. Redstone locks filling and draining, including remote relays.\n4. A comparator reads fullness.\n5. Spring Calling can mark a cistern as a spring so it refills itself.",
            "WIRELESS CARGO\n\nSnap a relay plate onto any face of a machine. Relays are for distance; hoppers and matching Output-into-Input faces are for neighbours.\n\nHow:\n1. Snap a Local, Longreach or Astral relay onto a face.\n2. Seat the same item in both Bond slots to pair them.\n3. Sneak-click a plate to switch extract or insert.\n4. Water Seal in the Rune slot moves fluid, Earth Seal moves items; empty uses the plate's name.\n5. The Lattice Tuner still marks a destination face, then links one plate. Hoppers cannot steal the Bond or Rune.",
            "CARGO TIERS\n\nThree distances. Rank the plate in Echo Attune, Bind, then Manifest to move more \u2014 and pay more Pulse.\n\nHow:\n1. Local relays reach 32 blocks. Cost 4 Pulse per successful beat.\n2. Longreach relays reach 128. Cost 8.\n3. Astral relays have no distance limit and can cross dimensions. Cost 16.\n4. Rank 1/2/3 pays 118% / 143% / 182% Pulse and moves that much more cargo (about 19 / 23 / 29 items, or 294 / 357 / 455 mB).\n5. Leave both ends loaded. Unloaded destinations pause; they do not void.",
            "CARGO RHYTHM\n\nEach second, a relay moves up to 16 items or 250 mB.\n\nHow:\n1. Pair the plates. Keep Pulse within 8 of the source plate.\n2. Both ends must already be loaded.\n3. Unloaded or full destinations pause safely.\n4. Relays never keep distant chunks loaded themselves \u2014 put a Wayanchor at the far end if it must keep working while you travel.\n5. Ranked plates move more per beat and spend more Pulse, so Pulse per item stays about even.",
            "CARGO CONTROLS\n\nA held signal stills the plate. A comparator tells you why.\n\nHow:\n1. Power the plate with redstone to pause it.\n2. Comparator: 0 unlinked, 1 linked but waiting, 15 transferring.\n3. Lock the receiver with redstone when you need a remote stop.\n4. Bound links survive pickup. The Bond item stays in the plate.\n5. Sneak-click to flip extract and insert without breaking the pair.",
            "PULSE TO FE\n\nThe Pulse Adapter translates harmony into standard energy.\n\nHow:\n1. Place the Adapter beside a generator and an FE machine.\n2. It converts 1 Pulse into 100 FE, up to 20 Pulse each second. Ranked adapters convert more Pulse, and more FE, in the same second.\n3. It buffers 16,000 FE and exports to standard energy receivers.\n4. Redstone stops conversion and extraction.\n5. A comparator reads the FE buffer.",
            "WAYSTONE PATHS\n\nA compass remembers a floor.\n\nHow:\n1. Sneak-use a compass on the top of a solid floor to bind a landing.\n2. Use it to return. Keep two clear dry blocks above the floor.\n3. Power the landing floor with redstone to lock arrival.\n4. Travel spends Pulse from a carried cell. A 5-second cooldown follows.\n5. If there is nowhere to stand, the trip refuses and the Pulse comes back.",
            "TRAVEL TIERS\n\nThree distances, one cooldown.\n\nHow:\n1. Waystone Compass: 128 blocks, same world, 20 Pulse.\n2. Horizon Compass: any distance in one world, 40 Pulse.\n3. Astral Compass: across dimensions, 100 Pulse.\n4. Bind a landing before you go. Keep two clear dry blocks above it.\n5. Travel has a 5-second cooldown. Redstone on the landing floor locks arrival.",
            "THE MARCH\n\nThe Gate Drum opens the way to The March. March materials unlock Astral transport, the Loom voice, and the last of the tablets.\n\nHow:\n1. Charge Pulse Cells. Bind a return compass.\n2. Place and strike a Gate Drum, or walk a Way Gate pair.\n3. Read every tablet in Ancestor Halls. The Codex records them.\n4. Strike a Silent Drum four beats, a breath apart, when you are ready for The Unsung.\n5. Bring March Crystal, Loom Thread and an Unsung Heart home. They open the sixth voice.",
            "SIXFOLD STAFF\n\nSneak-use to choose a voice; use to cast.\n\nHow:\n1. Craft the staff. Carry a charged Pulse Cell.\n2. Sneak-use to cycle Earth, Fire, Water, Air, Spirit, Loom.\n3. Use to cast. Earth slows foes. Fire strikes and ignites. Water heals and cleanses. Air grants a short leap and slow falling. Spirit reveals nearby enemies. Loom tethers a foe toward you or, sneaking with no target, stitches you 6 blocks forward.\n4. Offensive spells target hostiles and stop at solid obstacles.\n5. Water rests 8 seconds; other voices rest 2.",
            "STAFF COSTS\n\nThe staff spends Pulse, not durability.\n\nHow:\n1. Earth 12, Fire 18, Water 24, Air 16, Spirit 20 Pulse.\n2. Loom 6 to tether, 10 to stitch.\n3. Keep a cell in your inventory. The staff drinks from it.\n4. If the cell is dry, the cast does not fire.\n5. Water rests for 8 seconds; other voices for 2.",
            "RESONANCE MAUL\n\nA 3-by-3 plane of stone, paid in Pulse.\n\nHow:\n1. Hold the maul in your main hand.\n2. Sneak-use a stone face to excavate a 3-by-3 plane.\n3. Each block costs 8 Pulse.\n4. Tool requirements and normal player block protection still apply.\n5. If Pulse runs out mid-swing, remaining blocks stay.",
            "SPIRITWEAVE\n\nCloth that remembers a totem.\n\nHow:\n1. Craft Spiritweave armor. Fresh pieces are diamond-hard, rank 0.\n2. Unlinked hood: night sight. Robe: resistance. Leggings: speed. Boots: slow falling when descending.\n3. Each active piece spends 2 Pulse every four seconds from a carried cell.\n4. Sneak-use a piece on a placed Resonance Totem with 40 Pulse to bind a voice (3 Pulse upkeep). The bound voice replaces the default boon.\n5. Rank the cloth in Echo Attune, Bind, then Manifest. Air boots only spend Pulse when Slow Falling is not already on you.",
            "SPIRITGEAR RANKS\n\nThe Echo stations teach cloth and iron the same three voices they taught the catalysts.\n\nHow:\n1. Craft Spiritgear or Spiritweave. Fresh pieces are diamond-hard, rank 0, 1024 durability.\n2. Seat a piece in Echo Attune (Fire totem) to raise rank 0 to 1.\n3. Seat it in Echo Bind (Water) for 1 to 2. Bind refuses rank 0.\n4. Seat it in Echo Manifest (Spirit) for 2 to 3. You cannot skip.\n5. Rank 1 cheapens Pulse by one. Rank 2 skips the extra hurt when starved. Rank 3 mines at netherite speed and often spares the edge even without Pulse.\n\nUnweave of a damaged tool still returns one Manifested Ingot and forgets rank and voice.",
            "TOTEM-BOUND GEAR\n\nSneak-use a piece on a placed Resonance Totem with 40 Pulse. The totem is not consumed; overwrite is allowed.\n\nHow:\n1. Place the totem. Carry a charged cell.\n2. Sneak-use the tool or armor on it. The action bar names the voice.\n3. Mixed sets are intended. The bound voice replaces the default armor boon.\n4. Earth picks open 3-by-3 stone; Fire smelts; Water silks; Air hastes; Spirit glints ores; Loom mines without Pulse.\n5. Loom needs a Loom totem. Empty-handed clicks still read the totem. Extra 3-by-3 blocks spend Pulse durability the same way as the first.",
            "MACHINE RANKS\n\nWorkshops learn the same three voices, at twice the cost.\n\nHow:\n1. Pick up the machine. Seat the item in Echo Attune (Fire), then Bind (Water), then Manifest (Spirit).\n2. Rank 1 runs at 85% time and draws 118% Pulse. Rank 2 at 70% time and 143% Pulse. Rank 3 at 55% time and 182% Pulse.\n3. Pulse per craft stays about even \u2014 the extra speed is paid on the lattice. Ranked generators hum harder. Relays move more, and pay more Pulse for the extra cargo. Camp hands beat faster at the same Pulse per move.\n4. Place it again. The rank rides on the block and on the item when you pick it up.",
            "SPIRIT CHARMS\n\nWorn seals. Three slots that Tribal Power owns \u2014 no other mod is required.\n\nHow:\n1. Craft a charm. Use it to wear it; sneak-use to open the three slots.\n2. Sky is creative flight. Ember is fire. Tide is breath and swim. Root is resistance. Lantern is sight. Spindle is luck and a Pulse refund. Ward turns aside projectiles. Hearth keeps you fed. Veil hides you while you sneak.\n3. Chorus starts silent. Sneak-use it on a Ritual Brazier with three different totems within 8 and 200 Pulse to bind every nearby voice. Extra sneak-uses on totems add voices.\n4. Worn cost is 2 Pulse per voice every two seconds. Unequip if the drum runs dry.",
            "RITUAL BRAZIER\n\nSeat a reusable elemental seal. With its matching totem and Pulse nearby, the brazier sustains a blessing.\n\nHow:\n1. Place the brazier. Place the matching totem within 8.\n2. Seat the seal. It is not consumed.\n3. Keep Pulse nearby. It spends 8 Pulse every two seconds for players within 6 blocks.\n4. A lever pauses it. Sneak empty-handed to recover the seal.\n5. Tablet rites want a circle of pedestals around this brazier \u2014 see Draw the circle.",
            "CAMP BLESSINGS\n\nEarth grants haste; Fire resists flame; Water regenerates; Air slows falls; Spirit grants night sight.\n\nHow:\n1. Seat the matching seal in a Ritual Brazier.\n2. Place that voice's totem within 8.\n3. Stand within 6 blocks. The blessing ticks while Pulse lasts.\n4. Redstone pauses the brazier. Stored Pulse is not dumped.\n5. Sneak empty-handed to recover the seal.",
            "REDSTONE LANGUAGE\n\nA held signal stills the work. A struck signal calls it once.\n\nHow:\n1. Hold a line high to pause workshops, conductors, resonators, collectors, relays, braziers, meshes, fonts, pedestals, gate keystones and every generator, and to lock storage and travel destinations.\n2. A rising edge is a call. Only devices that do a discrete thing listen: a Drumheart takes a beat, a Ritual Brazier fires its seated rite, a keystone lights or darkens.\n3. Song Thread carries 0 to 15 weakly, like dust \u2014 it will not latch on stone.\n4. Song plates output from the facing. Unary plates read the back; binary plates read left and right.\n5. Nothing is ever lost to a pause.",
            "READ THE CAMP\n\nComparators tell you what a machine is holding without opening it.\n\nHow:\n1. Put a comparator against the block, facing away from it.\n2. They read stored Pulse, inventory or fluid fullness, FE buffer, and relay activity.\n3. A pause keeps stored resources intact.\n4. Use clocks, levers and comparators to choreograph the camp.\n5. Sneak-use the Codex if the number is not enough and you want a sentence.",
            "OTHER WORKSHOPS\n\nLattice recipes use the normal recipe manager and sync to clients.\n\nHow:\n1. Open JEI when it is installed. Every Echo station lists time, Pulse and voice.\n2. Datapacks can add tribalpower:lattice recipes using shared ingredient tags.\n3. Missing voices pause work. Full output pauses work. A lever pauses insert and work.\n4. Sit stations Output-into-Input to walk a chain without hoppers.\n5. Relays are for distance.",
            "THE VEIL AT NIGHT\n\nAfter dusk, the sky unfolds in slow curtains of green and violet.\n\nHow:\n1. Wait for night in the Overworld. The March carries a colder sky.\n2. Rain veils the aurora.\n3. Client settings can reduce its detail or disable it for shader packs.\n4. It is the sky trying to remember a schedule. It does not give Pulse by itself \u2014 a Ley Collector under that sky does.",
            "GENTLE HARVESTING\n\nBrush adult Dawn Stags, Lantern Foxes and Mossbacks for renewable reagents.\n\nHow:\n1. Find an adult. Young animals do not yield materials.\n2. Use an empty hand to brush. Each rests for one minute between harvests.\n3. Breed with wheat (stag), sweet berries (fox) and seagrass (mossback).\n4. Bond an adult with a Bonding Charm to double the reagent and keep a companion.\n5. Use Recipes in this Codex to follow the reagent into your workshop.",
            "BROKEN GUARDIANS\n\nAshbound, Rootbound and Reed Stalkers haunt forests and marshes in the Overworld. All can also be found in the March.\n\nHow:\n1. Build lighted paths. Hostile creatures require darkness.\n2. Keep water close to Ashbound. Rootbound roots you; wait it out. Reed Stalkers poison \u2014 milk or distance.\n3. Their reagents attune into two Attuned Echoes under Spirit.\n4. A Hush Totem or Still Night keeps a camp from growing a new pack overnight.\n5. Field notes live on each creature's own page.",
            "BEYOND THE GATE\n\nThe March biomes keep different remnants.\n\nHow:\n1. Steppe: Ashbound, Rootbound, Rift Hounds and Echo Weavers. Yellow pad-runners graze here.\n2. Highlands: Hollow Sentinels, Storm Moths, Cinder Imps and Rift Hounds. Drum Circles stand here. Mountain birds lean Great.\n3. Crystal Fields: Shardbacks, Mourning Bells, Reed Stalkers and Echo Weavers. The Crystal Spire is the Loom-stitcher camp.\n4. Snow Fields: Wonderful yellows on cold pads. Ember Wastes: Flame birds, Spark's old fire. Reed Fen: gysahl thickets and river-side yellows.\n5. Bind a return compass. Ester the Square Steward waits at Clowder Hall only after you have walked the March.",
            "ANSWERING A SPELL\n\nStorm Moths, Cinder Imps and Mourning Bells gather visible motes before casting.\n\nHow:\n1. Watch for the gathering. That is your warning.\n2. Step behind solid cover to interrupt. The spell never burns or replaces terrain.\n3. A charged staff is useful for keeping distance.\n4. Sneak against The Unsung's shockwave; that is a different fight, on its own page.\n5. Their reagents bind or attune like any other remnant.",
            "RETURNING THE SONG\n\nBring creature reagents to the Echo workshops.\n\nHow:\n1. Gentle animal harvests, Storm Wings and Echo Silk bind into Spiritweave under Water.\n2. Other hostile remnants attune into two Attuned Echoes under Spirit.\n3. Existing recipes remain available. JEI lists them.\n4. Rootbinders favour Mossback Scale. Colony-keepers favour Lantern Down. Offer what you brush.\n5. A bonded familiar sheds double, once a minute.",
            "WAYANCHOR\n\nSustain the chunk containing the anchor for 16 Pulse each second.\n\nHow:\n1. Place the anchor in the chunk that must stay loaded \u2014 a distant relay endpoint, a pit, a gate.\n2. Keep Pulse nearby. A 2,400-Pulse reserve bridges interruptions; nearby generators refill it.\n3. The anchor holds one chunk, not a radius. Up to 32 anchors may run per dimension (twelve if you share a camp).\n4. Redstone or an empty reserve releases its ticket. Removing the block releases it immediately.\n5. Place another at the other end of a relay if both ends must keep working while you travel.",
            "HUSH TOTEM\n\nA quiet circle suppresses hostile spawning within 24 blocks for 8 Pulse per second.\n\nHow:\n1. Place the totem in the middle of camp.\n2. Keep Pulse nearby. It covers natural and spawner-born hostiles, including Summoning Cradles.\n3. It does not remove existing mobs, stop animals, or override commands and spawn eggs.\n4. Redstone silences the ward immediately.\n5. Keep a cradle outside the circle, or use redstone to alternate between peace and summoning.",
            "GROVE TENDER\n\nThe Grove Tender keeps a living bed.\n\nHow:\n1. Place it at crop height in the middle of a 9-by-9 plot.\n2. Hopper seeds, saplings, cane, berries, nether wart or cocoa beans into the top row.\n3. Keep Pulse nearby: 4 to plant, 12 to harvest, 16 to urge a sapling, stem, crop or berry bush to grow.\n4. Pull harvests from below. Full output leaves the plant standing.\n5. A lever pauses work and inventory.\n\nIt plants and harvests wheat-family crops, nether wart, cocoa, sweet berries, sugar cane, cactus and bamboo, then takes logs and leaves in a 9-wide, 11-tall column. One job each second. Player protection still applies.",
            "BINDING EFFIGY\n\nAn empty or exhausted effigy remembers a living spirit without harming it.\n\nHow:\n1. Craft an empty Binding Effigy.\n2. Sneak-use it on an eligible animal or hostile creature.\n3. Common farm animals, zombies, skeletons, spiders, creepers and the thirteen Tribal Power creatures can be imprinted. Bosses cannot.\n4. A live binding cannot be overwritten.\n5. An imprint alone has no summons: awaken it through the Three-voice Binding.",
            "THREE-VOICE BINDING\n\nThe recipe is deliberately a ritual, not a spawn-egg shortcut.\n\nHow:\n1. Seat a Spirit Seal in a Ritual Brazier.\n2. Place Earth, Air and Spirit Totems within eight blocks.\n3. Supply 200 nearby Pulse and carry three Spiritweave.\n4. Use your imprinted, exhausted effigy on the brazier with redstone off. The three voices knot 512 summoning threads into it.\n5. Renew an exhausted effigy the same way, or first imprint another eligible spirit.",
            "SUMMONING CRADLE\n\nPlace a bound effigy in the first slot and Spiritweave in the second.\n\nHow:\n1. Every ten seconds the cradle attempts one summon on a clear, dry floor within three blocks.\n2. A successful summon costs 80 Pulse, one Spiritweave and one bound thread.\n3. Eight nearby mobs within twelve blocks pause it. Hostiles cannot be called in Peaceful or inside a Hush ward.\n4. Failed or blocked attempts spend nothing. A comparator reads remaining threads. Redstone pauses everything.\n5. Bottom automation can retrieve an exhausted effigy for renewal. Picking up the cradle drops the same effigy with its remaining count intact.",
            "SPIRIT LANTERN\n\nA carved copper-and-wood lantern brightens the camp at light level 15 without fuel.\n\nHow:\n1. Place it along paths between workshops.\n2. Redstone dims it.\n3. A comparator reports whether it is lit.\n4. Its animated crystal shares the living-lattice palette.\n5. No Pulse is needed.",
            "RAIN CHIME\n\nHang the idea of rain in copper.\n\nHow:\n1. Place the chime where a comparator can read it.\n2. It sounds softly every ten seconds during rain.\n3. Comparator: 8 for rain, 15 for thunder, 0 for clear skies.\n4. Redstone mutes it and sets its output to zero.\n5. Use the weather signal to choreograph Ley collection and camp lights. No fuel is needed.",
            "OFFERING TABLE\n\nA low carved display table doubles as a 27-slot store.\n\nHow:\n1. Place it beside a hearth or a cradle.\n2. Hoppers and item pipes can insert or extract from every side.\n3. A comparator reads fullness.\n4. Redstone locks both the menu and automation.\n5. No Pulse is needed for storage.",
            "THE SIXTH VOICE\n\nThe sixth voice is the thread itself. Loom Thread comes from Ancestor Halls and The Unsung.\n\nHow:\n1. Loot an Ancestor Hall for Loom Thread. Read the tablets.\n2. Wake The Unsung for an Unsung Heart.\n3. Craft the Loom totem: Unsung Heart, two threads, four March Crystals and two March Planks.\n4. Echo Unweave reverses the lattice: ingots to echoes, cores to ingots, Spiritweave to wool, and damaged Spiritgear to one Manifested Ingot.\n5. A Loom Seal in a Brazier threads 2 Pulse into carried cells every 2 seconds with Luck. The Sixfold Staff gains Tether and, sneaking with no target, Stitch.",
            "BONDED SPIRITS\n\nA companion that follows, waits, and sheds double reagent.\n\nHow:\n1. Craft a Bonding Charm from two Spiritweave, a Spirit Shard and a Lantern Down, Mossback Scale or Dawn Velvet.\n2. Use it on an adult of that species. Three tries in five succeed with hearts; a failed charm is kept.\n3. It follows within ten blocks, teleports to you past twelve, never despawns, and ignores your blows.\n4. Sneak-use it to make it wait or follow again.\n5. Brush it once a minute for double reagent.",
            "LANTERN FOX FAMILIAR\n\nA bonded Lantern Fox lights the way.\n\nHow:\n1. Bond an adult fox with a charm that includes Lantern Down.\n2. An invisible Spirit Light travels with it.\n3. Night Vision while you stay within eight blocks.\n4. Every four seconds it marks ores within six blocks of itself with glints only you can see.\n5. Colony-keepers favour Lantern Down at the hearth.",
            "MOSSBACK AND DAWN STAG FAMILIARS\n\nOne carries. One carries you.\n\nHow:\n1. Bond an adult Mossback: sneak-use with an empty hand for a nine-slot saddlebag; sneak-use holding an item to make it wait or follow. It drops the bag on death.\n2. Bond an adult Dawn Stag: use it to mount, no saddle. Steer with your gaze, hold jump for a short leap, sneak to dismount. It carries only the one it is bonded to.\n3. Rootbinders favour Mossback Scale.\n4. Brush either for double reagent.\n5. Young animals cannot be bonded.",
            "SHARED CAMPS\n\nA named camp with one vault, shared devices and pooled standing.\n\nHow:\n1. /tribalpower camp create <name>. You become its first member.\n2. Invite with /tribalpower camp invite <player> or a Camp Charter (paper, Spiritweave, Spirit Shard). Accept with /tribalpower camp join <name>. Invitations last five minutes.\n3. Open any Deep Cache or Wayfarer Satchel; sneak-use switches between your personal vault and the shared 54-slot camp vault.\n4. Members count as owners of each other's camp devices. The camp shares twelve Wayanchors per dimension instead of thirty-two each.\n5. A quarter of every member's tribe standing lands on the camp. Leave, kick, rename and info complete the command.",
            "WORLD RITES\n\nCarve a Rite Tablet from two stone, a creature reagent and the matching seal; the seal is handed back.\n\nHow:\n1. Sneak-use the tablet on a Ritual Brazier holding that seal, inside its circle.\n2. The brazier draws the rite's Pulse from the lattice within 8 blocks. If there is not enough, nothing is spent.\n3. Rain Calling (Water, 400) brings twenty minutes of rain.\n4. Sky Clearing (Air, 400) clears forty minutes.\n5. Dawn Calling (Fire, 800) hurries the night to sunrise unless the game rule tribalpower:allowDawnRite is off.",
            "LAND RITES\n\nAsk the ground, politely, for an exception.\n\nHow:\n1. Green Blessing (Earth, 600) blesses the nine chunks around the brazier for twenty minutes: crops, saplings and stems there take extra random ticks and sparkle green.\n2. Still Night (Spirit, 600) hushes hostile spawning within 64 blocks for fifteen minutes, like a wide Hush Totem. Seal-carvers sell this tablet to Friends.\n3. Ley Binding (Loom, 1,200) ties the brazier's nearest Resonance Totem to another within 64 blocks for thirty minutes.\n4. A Conductor routes Pulse along the humming thread as if the totems stood side by side.\n5. Draw the circle first. Missing pedestals fail the cast without spending the tablet.",
            "LEY LENS\n\nA glass pane, a Copper Resonator and a Spirit Shard make a lens for ley sight.\n\nHow:\n1. Hold it in either hand and use it to cycle four sights: ley strength on the ground (blue quiet, gold singing), the Pulse zone, nearby totem voices, and Tribal machines.\n2. Open sky, night, rain, water, plants, totem voices, hearths, animals, storm, moon and The March each add. The collector surveys 8 blocks; the lens paints 17 by 17.\n3. Sneak-use the lens on a Ley Collector to print that collector's exact factor breakdown.\n4. Voice mode tints totems gold when answered, dull when dim, grey when quiet.\n5. A roof starves a collector. A strong pad keeps nearby totems answered.",
            "PULSE LOGIC\n\nThe Gauge and Threshold still listen to Pulse. Song Thread and the thirteen song plates listen to redstone.\n\nHow:\n1. Point a Pulse Gauge at a Drumheart, Resonator or cell-holding machine. It emits 0 to 15 from every face except the arrow.\n2. Point a Pulse Threshold the same way. Empty-handed use cycles 25, 50, 75, 100 percent.\n3. Run Song Thread between plates. Power decays by one per block, in all six directions.\n4. Snap a song plate onto a face. The facing is the output. Left and right are the two inputs; the back is the unary input.\n5. Sneak-use Heartbeat, Drift or Tally plates to change their timing.\n\nA factory is a song that has stopped needing the singer.",
            "CODEX DIAGNOSTICS\n\nSneak-use the Spirit Codex on any Tribal block to hear it explain itself.\n\nHow:\n1. Sneak-use this book on the silent block.\n2. It names stored Pulse, every generator within 8 blocks with its output this second, the attunements present, the Pulse it could draw, and whether redstone pauses it.\n3. Workshops name their recipe and any missing voice or full output.\n4. Relays report unloaded or locked endpoints. Braziers list the rites their seal allows.\n5. Pattern anchors also show ghosts of missing pieces.",
            "STANDING\n\nNine tribes kept the Loom, one Strand each; their camps still keep time.\n\nHow:\n1. Find a camp: hearth, banner, four Kin.\n2. Offer a favoured item at the Tribe Hearth for +3, the tribe's reagent for +8, any food for +1, or a charged Pulse Cell for +2 per 10 Pulse.\n3. Hostile kills within 24 blocks of a hearth give +1, twenty per day per tribe. A trade gives +2.\n4. Ranks: Guest 50, Friend 150, Kin 400, Voice 800. Hurting Kin costs 25 and turns the camp's Hunters on you for a minute; breaking a hearth costs 40.\n5. /tribalpower standing prints all nine.",
            "TRIBAL KIN\n\nEvery camp keeps four Kin.\n\nHow:\n1. Elder: trades from the tribe's table once you are a Guest. Two offers per rank. At Voice, presses a Tribe Mark into your hand.\n2. Drummer: every few seconds feeds 2 Pulse into generators within 8 blocks.\n3. Hunter: strikes hostiles within 12 blocks. Hits you for a minute if you hurt Kin.\n4. Weaver: stands at the loom.\n5. Kin wander within 16 blocks of their camp and never despawn. Never hit them.",
            "KINSHIP TOTEM\n\nAn extra voice for the Resonator, tracked per tribe rather than per element.\n\nHow:\n1. Reach Voice with a tribe. The Elder presses a Tribe Mark into your hand.\n2. Craft the Mark with that tribe's Resonance Totem and two Spiritweave.\n3. Place the Kinship Totem within 8 of a station or Resonator.\n4. It lends the tribe's voice and counts as an extra distinct voice.\n5. Nine tribes beside six totems make fifteen voices.",
            "PAD-KEEPERS\n\nStrand of Soil, voice of Earth. Craft: hearths and caches. Camps stand in plains; a March camp keeps the old road. Favoured offerings: dirt, moss, bread and Echo Shards.\n\n\"We never called it dirt. We called it what was left, and we kept it warm.\"",
            "GRIT-SINGERS\n\nStrand of Stone, voice of Earth. Craft: echo shatter and meshes. Camps stand in mountains; a March camp keeps the old road. Favoured offerings: raw ores, grits and Attuned Echo.\n\n\"The mesh does not find the ore. The mesh gives the ore somewhere to land.\"",
            "ROOTBINDERS\n\nStrand of Sprout, voice of Water. Craft: living anchors and March flora. Camps stand in forests; a March camp keeps the old road. Favoured offerings: saplings, seeds and Mossback Scale.\n\n\"Roots are the only rope the void respects.\"",
            "EDGE-WALKERS\n\nStrand of Claw, voice of Fire. Craft: Spiritgear and footholds. Camps stand in taiga; a March camp keeps the old road. Favoured offerings: leather, iron and Rift Tooth.\n\n\"Boots first. Then the bridge. Then the courage; it arrives on its own.\"",
            "DRUMHEARTS\n\nStrand of Spark, voice of Fire. Craft: drums and Pulse. Camps stand in savanna; a March camp keeps the old road. Favoured offerings: copper, charged Pulse Cells and Bone Chimes.\n\n\"The drum is not loud. The drum is steady. Be the drum.\"",
            "PATTERN-WEAVERS\n\nStrand of Clock, voice of Air. Craft: timed songs and automation. Camps stand in birch woods; a March camp keeps the old road. Favoured offerings: redstone, clocks and Storm Wing.\n\n\"A factory is a song that has stopped needing the singer.\"",
            "COLONY-KEEPERS\n\nStrand of Swarm, voice of Air. Craft: hives and March flowers. Camps stand in flower meadows; a March camp keeps the old road. Favoured offerings: honey, flowers and Lantern Down.\n\n\"You do not own a hive. You are on good terms with it.\"",
            "SEAL-CARVERS\n\nStrand of Sigil, voice of Spirit. Craft: seals and rites. Camps stand in dark forests; a March camp keeps the old road. Favoured offerings: blank or element seals and Spirit Shards.\n\n\"Spirit goes where it is asked politely and stays where it is fed.\"",
            "LOOM-STITCHERS\n\nStrand of Spindle, voice of Loom. Craft: gate-paths and the reweave. Camps stand in the March crystal fields only; a March camp keeps the old road. Favoured offerings: March Crystal, Loom Thread and compasses.\n\n\"The Loom was never one thread. It was nine agreeing.\"",
            "ANCESTOR HALL\n\nSunken stone halls in the March steppe and highlands.\n\nHow:\n1. Find a hall: three rooms under Loom-wood beams with a ladder shaft to the surface.\n2. Read every Lore Tablet on the walls. The Codex records them.\n3. Two chests hold Loom Thread, echoes, Spiritweave and seals.\n4. Hollow Sentinels keep the side rooms \u2014 light and a staff help.\n5. Next: a Drum Circle in the highlands, and the Crystal Spire for Loom-stitcher trades.",
            "DRUM CIRCLE\n\nTwelve lantern-topped pillars ring a Silent Drum in the March highlands.\n\nHow:\n1. Bind a return compass. Bring food, Pulse and a Bone Chime.\n2. Strike the drum empty-handed or with a Bone Chime: four beats about a second apart (16 to 28 ticks).\n3. A wrong beat thuds and resets. Each drum answers once per twenty minutes of real time, and never while its keeper is already awake.\n4. A music disc of the circle's four-beat sits in a chest among the pillars; The Unsung carries another.\n5. See Walkthrough: wake The Unsung for the fight itself.",
            "THE UNSUNG\n\nA hollow drum-spirit with two rune arms and a cracked mask. It only wants the rhythm back.\n\nHow:\n1. Beat (above two thirds): a shockwave every 3 seconds hits everyone within 8 blocks for 6 and knocks back. Sneak to brace for half damage and no knockback. Its swipe deals 10.\n2. Chorus: every 8 seconds it calls two Echo Weavers, up to six, and beats faster. Clear the weavers.\n3. Silence (below one third): invulnerable over the drum, slow weaving bolts. Play the four-beat on the Silent Drum to resync: stunned 8 seconds at double damage. Silence returns 12 seconds after each resync.\n4. Drops an Unsung Heart, 16 to 24 Loom Thread, 4 Resonant Cores, and a Drum Circle music disc.\n5. Leave for 30 seconds and it resets.",
            "CRYSTAL SPIRE\n\nA tapering spire of March Crystal in the crystal fields.\n\nHow:\n1. Find the waystation at its foot: a hearth, a banner, a Loom totem and one Elder of the Spindle tribe.\n2. Offer March Crystal, Loom Thread or compasses.\n3. Friend standing opens Loom Thread trades.\n4. This is the only camp the Loom-stitchers keep.\n5. Bind a compass before you wander the crystal fields \u2014 Shardbacks shove hard.",
            "TABLET: PAD-KEEPERS' HEARTH\n\nWe never called it dirt. We called it what was left, and we kept it warm. When the ground fell away we carried it in baskets, a pad at a time, and set a hearth on every pad we saved. Feed the hearth bread and moss. It remembers who fed it.",
            "TABLET: GRIT-SINGERS' MESH\n\nThe mesh does not find the ore. The mesh gives the ore somewhere to land. Sing low over raw stone and it loosens; sing lower and it shatters into echo. Our meshes still hang in the halls, humming to nothing. Bring them ore and they will hum to you.",
            "TABLET: ROOTBINDERS' ROPE\n\nRoots are the only rope the void respects. We planted the first anchors on the falling islands and bound them island to island, root to root. Half of them held. Plant a sapling in the March soil and you will feel it pull toward the others.",
            "TABLET: EDGE-WALKERS' BOOTS\n\nBoots first. Then the bridge. Then the courage; it arrives on its own. We walked the rift edge where the thread frayed thinnest and set footholds for the rest. A foothold is iron, leather and a promise not to look down.",
            "TABLET: DRUMHEARTS' BEAT\n\nThe drum is not loud. The drum is steady. Be the drum. One beat a breath apart, and the copper answers; miss a beat and it forgets you. Every engine in the March still keeps our time. Strike, wait, strike. That is the whole of it.",
            "TABLET: PATTERN-WEAVERS' SONG\n\nA factory is a song that has stopped needing the singer. We wrote the timings on clock-wheels and moth dust and let the Loom carry the tune. When the Cut came the songs kept playing. Some are playing still. Listen for the click before the hum.",
            "TABLET: COLONY-KEEPERS' HIVE\n\nYou do not own a hive. You are on good terms with it. Offer honey, plant the March flowers, and the swarm will route Pulse through the comb for you. Take without asking and the comb goes quiet. It is very patient about this.",
            "TABLET: SEAL-CARVERS' RITE\n\nSpirit goes where it is asked politely and stays where it is fed. A seal is a polite request carved in stone. A brazier is the meal. We cut blank seals by the thousand before the Cut, and asked for far too much. Ask for a little. Feed it well.",
            "TABLET: LOOM-STITCHERS' THREAD\n\nThe Loom was never one thread. It was nine agreeing. We held the Spindle and stitched the tribes' strands into one cloth over the sky. When eight pulls became eight arguments, the cloth tore along our seam. We are still stitching. Bring crystal. Bring thread.",
            "TABLET: THE CUT\n\nNo one struck the Loom. It was pulled from nine sides until one strand gave, and then the rest went like a rope through a hand. The continents fell in the space of a drum-roll. What did not fall drifted into the March and sank slow. Nine tribes, one hall, no one to blame.",
            "TABLET: THE UNSUNG\n\nA drum was carried out of every falling camp so the beat would not stop. The last drum was carried into the circle and no one was left to strike it. Its keeper went hollow waiting. Wake it with the four-beat and it will rise to be struck. Sneak when it beats. Resync it when it goes silent. It only wants the rhythm back.",
            "TABLET: THE MARCH\n\nThe March is where the thread frayed thinnest and the fallen ground came to rest. Halls lie sunk to the lintel; camps keep time with no one at the drum; crystal grows where the Loom's tension still pools. Walk it with a full Pulse cell and a steady hand. Everything here still answers a beat.",
            "WALKTHROUGH: YOUR FIRST CAMP\n\n1. Find a tribe camp: a hearth, a banner and four Kin in plains, mountains, forest, taiga, savanna, birch woods, flower meadows or dark forest. The banner colour names the tribe; the tribe pages list what each favours.\n2. Read the hearth. Sneak-use the Spirit Codex on it, or simply watch what the Kin carry: bread and moss for Pad-keepers, ores for Grit-singers, saplings for Rootbinders.\n3. Offer. Use a favoured item on the Tribe Hearth for +3 standing, or the tribe's reagent for +8. Any food gives +1 and a charged Pulse Cell gives +2 per 10 Pulse. Seventeen favoured offerings, or seven reagents, reach Guest at 50.\n4. Trade. Use the Elder once you are a Guest. Every trade gives +2, and each rank unlocks two more offers.\n5. Keep the peace. Never hit Kin (-25 standing and an angry Hunter for a minute) and never break the hearth (-40). Kills of hostiles within 24 blocks of the hearth earn +1, twenty times a day.\nWhat you now have: Guest standing with one tribe, its first trades, and a hearth that remembers you. /tribalpower standing prints all nine.\nNext: Friend at 150 opens the seal and tablet trades; Voice at 800 earns a Tribe Mark, the key to a Kinship Totem.",
            "WALKTHROUGH: THE SIXTH VOICE\n\n1. Loot an Ancestor Hall. The sunken halls in the March steppe and highlands keep Loom Thread in their two chests; read the four tablets on the way out.\n2. Carve a Loom Seal: a Blank Seal, one Loom Thread and a Spirit Shard, shapeless. Seat it in a Ritual Brazier with Pulse nearby to thread 2 Pulse into your carried cells every two seconds.\n3. Build Echo Unweave: March Stone around a Copper Resonator, a Spirit Shard and two Loom Thread. It needs the Loom voice within 8 blocks, which for now only a Kinship Totem of the Loom-stitchers or a Loom-stitcher camp can lend.\n4. Wake The Unsung at a Drum Circle (see that walkthrough) and take its Unsung Heart.\n5. Craft the Loom totem: four March Crystal, two Loom Thread, two March Planks around the Unsung Heart. Place it within 8 blocks of the Unweave and of a Pulse Resonator.\nWhat you now have: the sixth voice. Unweave turns ingots back to echoes, cores to ingots, Spiritweave to wool and damaged Spiritgear into one Manifested Ingot; the Resonator counts one more distinct voice.\nNext: the Sixfold Staff's Loom voice (Tether and Stitch) and the Ley Binding rite, which needs the Loom seal.",
            "WALKTHROUGH: WAKE THE UNSUNG\n\n1. Prepare: full Pulse cells, food, a Bone Chime, and a bound return route. Bring a friend if you can; the fight lasts a few minutes.\n2. Find a Drum Circle in the March highlands: twelve lantern pillars around a Silent Drum.\n3. Beat four times. Strike the drum empty-handed or with the chime, about one second apart (16 to 28 ticks). A wrong beat thuds and resets the count. The drum answers once per twenty minutes and never while its keeper is awake.\n4. Beat phase: every three seconds a shockwave hits everyone within 8 blocks for 6 and knocks back. Sneak just before it lands to brace: half damage, no knockback. Its swipe deals 10, so keep the drum between you.\n5. Chorus, below two thirds health: it calls two Echo Weavers every eight seconds, up to six, and beats faster. Clear the weavers before they slow you.\n6. Silence, below one third: it hovers invulnerable over the drum and casts slow weaving bolts. Walk to the drum and play the four-beat again to resync it: eight seconds stunned at double damage. Silence returns twelve seconds after each resync, so repeat.\nWhat you now have: an Unsung Heart, 16 to 24 Loom Thread, 4 Resonant Cores, and a Drum Circle music disc. Leaving for thirty seconds resets the fight.\nNext: the Loom totem (The sixth voice) and the Loom-stitcher trades at the Crystal Spire.",
            "WALKTHROUGH: YOUR FIRST RITE\n\n1. Choose the rite. Rain Calling needs the Water seal and 400 Pulse; Sky Clearing the Air seal and 400. Dawn Calling (Fire, 800) and the land rites cost more. Start with rain.\n2. Carve the tablet: two stone, the rite's creature reagent (a Reed Fang for rain) and the matching seal, shapeless. The seal is handed back.\n3. Seat the seal. Use the Water Seal on a Ritual Brazier; the brazier's usual blessing still runs, and the seal stays reusable.\n4. Gather 400 Pulse within 8 blocks of the brazier: a charged Greater Pulse Cell in a Drumheart, a Resonator with a good catalyst, or several generators together. A Pulse Gauge or the Codex diagnostics show the total.\n5. Cast. Sneak-use the tablet on the brazier. If the lattice holds less than the cost nothing is spent; otherwise the tablet is consumed and the Pulse drawn.\nWhat you now have: twenty minutes of rain (or forty minutes of clear sky), stronger Ley Collectors, and a brazier that knows how to answer tablets.\nNext: Green Blessing over your farm (Earth, 600), Still Night around the camp (Spirit, 600), or Ley Binding between two distant totems (Loom, 1,200).",
            "WALKTHROUGH: BOND A FAMILIAR\n\n1. Craft a Bonding Charm: two Spiritweave, a Spirit Shard and one reagent of the animal you want (Lantern Down, Mossback Scale or Dawn Velvet). Brush an adult of that species to get the reagent.\n2. Find an adult Lantern Fox (forests, dusk), Mossback (swamps) or Dawn Stag (forests, dawn). Young animals cannot be bonded.\n3. Use the charm on it. Three tries in five succeed with hearts; a failed charm is kept, so try again.\n4. Follow and stay. The familiar follows within ten blocks and teleports to you past twelve. Sneak-use it (empty-handed for a Mossback) to make it wait, and again to follow. It never despawns and ignores your blows.\n5. Learn its trick. Fox: an invisible Spirit Light travels with it, Night Vision within eight blocks, and ore glints only you can see. Mossback: sneak-use with an empty hand for a nine-slot saddlebag. Stag: use it to ride without a saddle, steer with your gaze, hold jump to leap, sneak to dismount.\n6. Brush it. A bonded animal sheds double reagent, once a minute.\nWhat you now have: a companion that lights, carries or carries you, and a renewable reagent supply.\nNext: Rootbinders favour Mossback Scale and Colony-keepers Lantern Down, so a brushed familiar also buys standing.",
            "WALKTHROUGH: SEAT A RESONATOR\n\n1. Craft Echo Shatter and an Earth Resonance Totem. Place the totem within 8 of the station.\n2. Feed stone, deepslate or March stone into Echo Shatter (top or sides). Take Echo Shards from below. Cobble is the hammer chain, not shards.\n3. Craft and place a Pulse Resonator. Right-click it with one Echo Shard. The action bar should say the catalyst is seated and not consumed.\n4. Place a second totem of a different voice within 8 blocks (Fire is the usual pair).\n5. Wait one second. The Resonator lights. Click it: you should see Pulse rising, about 6 a second with two voices and a shard.\n6. Optional: sneak empty-handed to lift the shard, seat a stronger catalyst later, or sneak-use the Codex if it stays dark.\nWhat you now have: a generator that runs without hitting a drum. Charge a Pulse Cell on it the same way you would a Drumheart.\nNext: Harmonic ranks for stronger crystals, and the Voice Ring if you want six voices.",
            "WALKTHROUGH: RUN A CONDUCTOR\n\n1. Place two Resonance Totems within 16 of each other, and a Drumheart (or Ley Collector, or Resonator) nearby.\n2. Hold Ritual Chalk. Click totem A, then totem B. You should see \"Lattice link sealed\". Clicking the same totem twice cancels the pending mark.\n3. Place a Lattice Conductor within 8 of those totems and within 8 of the generator.\n4. Put Pulse in the generator: strike the Drumheart, or seat a catalyst in the Resonator.\n5. Wait one second, or click the Conductor. It should report a lattice network and Pulse routed into totem buffers.\n6. If a Song Bench on the lattice wants help, the Conductor fills it first. Ancestral Caches beside the totems will swap Echo items with benches every two seconds while Pulse is present.\n7. A lever on the Conductor pauses it. Sneak-use the Spirit Codex on it to hear network size, last Pulse pushed, and what is missing.\nWhat you now have: Pulse walking from your generators into totems and workshops instead of sitting in one drum.\nNext: Ley Binding to join distant totems, and wireless relays when you need items rather than Pulse.",
            "WALKTHROUGH: TOTEM-BOUND GEAR\n\n1. Craft Spiritgear (Manifested Ingots) or Spiritweave armor. Fresh pieces are diamond-hard, rank 0, unlinked.\n2. Carry a charged Pulse Cell (40 Pulse to link).\n3. Place a Resonance Totem. Sneak-use the piece on it. The action bar names the voice. Empty-handed clicks still read the totem.\n4. Rank it: Echo Attune with a Fire totem (0 to 1), Echo Bind with Water (1 to 2), Echo Manifest with Spirit (2 to 3). Bind refuses rank 0; you cannot skip.\n5. Mix voices if you want: a Fire hood is fire resist, not night sight. A full linked set costs 12 Pulse every four seconds.\n6. Loom voice needs a Loom totem (see The sixth voice). Unweave of a damaged tool returns one Manifested Ingot and forgets rank and voice.\nWhat you now have: gear that answers a totem, and a rank path through the Echo stations.\nNext: JEI lists every rank formula. Totem-bound gear in this Codex names the tool perks.",
            "WALKTHROUGH: FOUND A CAMP\n\n1. Found it: /tribalpower camp create <name>. You become its first member.\n2. Invite. Craft a Camp Charter (paper, Spiritweave, Spirit Shard) and use it on a player, or run /tribalpower camp invite <player>. Invitations last five minutes; the invitee accepts with /tribalpower camp join <name>.\n3. Share the vault. Open any Deep Cache or Wayfarer Satchel: sneak-use switches between your personal vault and the shared 54-slot camp vault.\n4. Share the devices. Members count as owners of each other's camp devices: cradles, tenders, anchors and locked menus open for all of you.\n5. Budget anchors. The camp shares twelve Wayanchors per dimension instead of thirty-two each, so agree on which chunks matter.\n6. Manage it: /tribalpower camp info, rename, kick and leave. A quarter of every member's tribe standing lands on the camp, and an Elder trades at the camp's rank when it beats your own.\nWhat you now have: a named camp with one vault, shared devices and pooled tribe standing.\nNext: the Shared camps teaching for the fine print, and Kinship Totems to lend your camp every tribe's voice.",
            "PLACEMENT IS THE RITUAL\n\nA device that claims to be a rite has to be arranged, not scattered.\n\nHow:\n1. Pick an anchor: Stone Font, Resonance Mesh, Ritual Brazier, Pulse Resonator, Echo station, or Gate Keystone.\n2. Build the pattern around it. Any rotation works.\n3. Sneak-use the Spirit Codex on the anchor.\n4. It names the tier, the facing, and the first three things that are missing, with ghosts where they should go.\n5. Brace corners with Anchor Stones when a tier asks for them.",
            "RITUAL MARK\n\nMarks are what join a pattern together.\n\nHow:\n1. Craft Ritual Chalk \u2014 four sticks, ten uses each.\n2. Click the top of a solid block to draw a mark. Each draw spends one use.\n3. Click the mark again to rub it out. Erasing costs nothing.\n4. Click two Resonance Totems (within 16) to seal a Lattice link; a successful link spends one use.\n5. Marks drop nothing when broken, because the chalk already paid.\n\nCreative mode does not spend uses.",
            "ANCHOR STONE\n\nThey brace the corners of a pattern and do nothing else: no Pulse, no inventory, no upkeep.\n\nHow:\n1. Craft four March Stone and an Echo Shard into four Anchor Stones.\n2. Place them on the corners the Codex ghosts show.\n3. A pattern that has them is a tier higher than one that does not.\n4. They are not generators. Leave them alone after they sit.\n5. Break one and the pattern drops a tier until you replace it.",
            "STONE FONT\n\nStone is not made. Stone is asked to stay. This is the only machine cheap enough to run on a hand-drummed Drumheart.\n\nHow:\n1. Craft four stone, two Echo Shards and a Drumheart into a font.\n2. Place it with four chalk marks around it: cobble every two seconds at 4 Pulse a second.\n3. Brace the corners with Anchor Stones and bring the Earth voice: stone at 16 Pulse a second.\n4. Add Fire and Water both: obsidian at 24 Pulse a second. Or feed 250 mB of water and 250 mB of lava into a braced Earth font for the same obsidian at 6.\n5. Below y 0 it gives the deepslate of each tier instead. Rank the font like any other workshop: faster asks, more Pulse a second, cobble per Pulse stays about even. Cobble from the font is for hammers and building, not Echo Shards.",
            "LISTENING PIT\n\nThe mesh does not find the ore. The mesh gives the ore somewhere to land.\n\nHow:\n1. Lay stone or deepslate in the pit footprint.\n2. Brace four corners with Anchor Stones. Chalk from each edge to the middle.\n3. Set a Resonance Mesh at the centre, an Ancestral Cache beside it, and the Earth voice within eight blocks.\n4. Hopper substrate in from the sides. Seat a sample on top. Take ore from the bottom \u2014 or let the mesh empty itself into the cache.\n5. Rank the mesh like any other workshop: faster cycles, more Pulse a second, ore per Pulse stays about even. Sneak-use the Codex on the mesh if a piece is missing.",
            "DEEP LISTENING\n\nThe seven by seven doubles the corner bracing and opens the deep, hot and rare bands.\n\nHow:\n1. Expand the pit to seven by seven. Double the corner bracing.\n2. Seat a totem at each cardinal edge.\n3. Stand a Tribe Hearth or a Grit-singer Kinship Totem inside the pattern.\n4. Grit-singer standing gates the bands: Friend for common, Kin for deep, Voice and their kinship for rare.\n5. Hot wants Fire. Rare wants Spirit. The Codex names what you still lack.",
            "WHAT THE GROUND OFFERS\n\nThe pit calls up exactly what a silk-touch mining trip would: the raw item for a metal, the ore block for a gem.\n\nHow:\n1. Common: coal, copper and iron at 10 seconds and 14 Pulse a second on two stone.\n2. Deep: gold, redstone, lapis and quartz at 15 seconds and 18, on two March Stone.\n3. Hot: the Nether's quartz and gold at 20 seconds and 36, with Fire.\n4. Rare: diamond, emerald and whatever a modded pack added, at 40 seconds and 24, on four March Stone and a Spirit Shard.\n5. Mining stays cheaper per ingot. The pit buys walking away.",
            "SAMPLE AND SUBSTRATE\n\nA sample is a filter, never an ingredient.\n\nHow:\n1. Seat a sample on top of the mesh. It is not consumed.\n2. A material it names weighs six times as much as anything else in the band.\n3. A sample the band does not hold is ignored, and the Codex says so.\n4. Substrates are renewable on purpose \u2014 stone from a Stone Font, March Stone from cobble.\n5. Per iron ingot the pit costs about 70 Pulse against 20 for shattering ore you mined.",
            "VOICES AT THE PIT\n\nEach voice trades one thing for another; none of them is a plain multiplier.\n\nHow:\n1. Earth is required.\n2. Water washes for 250 mB a cycle and gives one extra output every third cycle.\n3. Air quickens the cycle to about two thirds and charges half again as much a second \u2014 Pulse per item does not move.\n4. Fire opens the hot band at twice the Pulse. Spirit listens a band deeper and opens the rare one.\n5. The Loom halves the substrate, rounded up.",
            "WAY GATE\n\nA five by five ring without its corners, keystone at the bottom centre.\n\nHow:\n1. Six March Stone, two copper and an Echo Shard make four Gate Frames.\n2. Four frames, a Resonant Core, a Spirit Shard and a Pulse Cell make the keystone.\n3. Build the ring. Charge the keystone from a Pulse Cell.\n4. Light it by hand or with a struck signal: 400 Pulse out of its own 600.\n5. Twenty Pulse carries anything that walks in \u2014 players, mobs and dropped items. That is bulk logistics.",
            "FAR GATE\n\nA taller frame around a three by four interior. Crossing dimensions sits behind The Unsung.\n\nHow:\n1. Build the taller ring. Brace four Anchor Stones at the corners of its footprint.\n2. Place the Loom voice within eight blocks.\n3. Craft a Gate Sigil: Blank Seal, Loom Thread and a Spirit Shard.\n4. Sneak-use the sigil on one keystone to write that gate down, then use it on the other to tie the pair both ways.\n5. Travel is 120 Pulse with a two-second breath afterwards.",
            "KEEPING THE WAY\n\nA gate always lands you inside the far gate's own interior and never terraforms.\n\nHow:\n1. Link Way Gates locally: sneak-use a bound Waystone Compass on a keystone, or draw chalk from one keystone to the other within 64 blocks.\n2. If there is nowhere to stand the trip refuses and the Pulse comes back.\n3. The far end is held loaded for ten seconds around your arrival, so an unloaded partner still answers.\n4. Break a keystone and its partner is released; anyone standing near it is told.\n5. /tribalpower gate list and /tribalpower gate unlink read and cut the threads.",
            "EMBER HORN\n\nThe Drumhearts' craft. Feed it furnace fuel.\n\nHow:\n1. Place the horn. Hopper, relay or hand-feed any furnace fuel.\n2. Burn time divided by twenty is Pulse, delivered at up to 20 a second.\n3. Coal is 80, a coal block 800, a lava bucket 1,000, a blaze rod 120.\n4. The rate is the real cap, so scaling means more horns \u2014 and horns are a tribe craft.\n5. Nothing you can automate turns fuel into more fuel than it burns.",
            "WIND HARP\n\nThe Pattern-weavers' craft, and free, so it is capped instead.\n\nHow:\n1. Place the harp under open sky. Under a roof it makes nothing at all.\n2. One Pulse a second as a base and one more under open sky.\n3. One more above y 128 and two above y 192. One more in rain or two in a storm.\n4. Six a second is the whole of the wind.\n5. Harps within twelve blocks divide it between them, so a wall of harps is a wall of decorations.",
            "WAVE DRUM\n\nThe Rootbinders' craft, and the second job for fluid transport.\n\nHow:\n1. Place it beside water for 3 Pulse a second, shared with any drum within eight blocks.\n2. Give it its own water instead \u2014 a bucket, a cistern, a fluid relay \u2014 and it makes 10 a second for 100 mB a second.\n3. Rain doubles either tier.\n4. Pair a Tide Pump if you need the water to move after it arrives.\n5. Spring Calling is how the cistern refills itself.",
            "WAKE BELL\n\nThe Seal-carvers' craft. A mob farm that pays Pulse.\n\nHow:\n1. Place the bell within sixteen blocks of the deaths.\n2. Twenty Pulse for a hostile death, five for a passive one.\n3. A reservoir of 2,000 lets out at most eight a second. A big farm fills it and then idles.\n4. Only the nearest bell hears a death, so stacking bells buys nothing.\n5. A Pulse Cairn turns those bursts into the steady draw a Listening Pit wants.",
            "LOOM ANCHOR\n\nThe Loom-stitchers' craft, and the one that pays for completeness.\n\nHow:\n1. Place the Anchor within eight blocks of your totems.\n2. One Pulse a second per distinct voice, to a maximum of six.\n3. A live Ley Binding nearby doubles it.\n4. It generates from the system itself, so it needs no cap of its own: there are only six voices.\n5. Rank it in Echo Attune, Bind, then Manifest to hum harder.",
            "PULSE CAIRN\n\nA stack of stone that holds a beat.\n\nHow:\n1. Craft six March Stone, two Bound Echoes and a Pulse Cell.\n2. Each cairn holds 4,000 Pulse and draws surplus out of nearby generators.\n3. Stack up to five in a column; the sixth stone is just a stone.\n4. A comparator reads how full it is.\n5. Sit one beside a Wake Bell and a Listening Pit so bursts become a steady draw.",
            "SPRING CALLING\n\nRain Calling's small sibling. The seal comes back.\n\nHow:\n1. Carve the tablet: two stone, a Spirit Reed and the Water Seal.\n2. Seat the Water Seal in a brazier. Place a Spirit Cistern beside it.\n3. Spend 300 Pulse. The cistern becomes a spring: 100 mB a second for ten minutes.\n4. Repeat when it runs dry. This is the water for Wave Drums, Washing and Tide Pumps.\n5. March-side lava stays a manual haul: the Ember Horn's best fuel should cost a trip.",
            "DRAW THE CIRCLE\n\nA brazier's blessing still needs nothing but a seated seal. A tablet rite now wants its circle.\n\nHow:\n1. Brazier in the middle.\n2. Four Rite Pedestals on the diagonals, chalk joining them.\n3. Seat four totems of the rite's own voice on the cardinals and it costs a quarter less and lasts twice as long.\n4. Sneak-use the Codex on the brazier if a pedestal is missing.\n5. This is the one deliberate change to something that already worked, and the failure message says so.",
            "A RITE ON A CLOCK\n\nA Rite Pedestal holds and shows one item. A comparator reads whether it is occupied.\n\nHow:\n1. A relay restocks a pedestal with a tablet.\n2. A Heartbeat plate (or a lever) strikes the brazier.\n3. The rite fires and spends the tablet.\n4. The comparator reports the pedestal empty, and the relay fills it again.\n5. No fake players, no hidden inventories \u2014 everything a player can do by hand, a base can do on a clock.",
            "METALS AND GEMS\n\nGrit means one thing now: crushed metal waiting for the fire.\n\nHow:\n1. Metal: raw item or silk-touched ore into Echo Shatter to grit, then grit to ingot in a furnace, blast furnace or Ember Kiln.\n2. Gem or mineral: silk-touched ore shatters straight into the gem at twice the ore's own drop.\n3. Coal, diamond, emerald and quartz give two. Redstone and lapis give eight. The gem itself is never an input.\n4. Modded metals ride one Mineral Grit item that names its own material, and light up with no datapack.\n5. Sit Shatter on a Kiln, Output into Input, and grit walks down.",
            "VOICE RING\n\nA heap of totems counts at most five voices. Six-voice resonance only counts when the voices are arranged.\n\nHow:\n1. Place the Resonator.\n2. On the same floor, three blocks away at the cardinals and diagonals, stand Resonance Totems (eight slots on a square grid).\n3. Seat a catalyst. Distinct voices among those arranged totems all count, including the sixth.\n4. Sneak-use the Spirit Codex on the Resonator to see ghosts of any missing ring slots.\n5. Totems merely near it still work exactly as they did for five voices.",
            "SHATTER ARRAY\n\nCentre an Echo station in a five by five with four totems of the recipe's own attunement at the corners and an Ancestral Cache beneath.\n\nHow:\n1. Place the station. Four matching totems at the corners of a five by five.\n2. Put an Ancestral Cache under it.\n3. The station then costs a quarter less Pulse and empties itself into the cache.\n4. Entirely optional. Every station works exactly as before without it.\n5. Sneak-use the Codex on the station to see the ghosts.",
            "CAMP HANDS\n\nPattern-weavers taught the camp to keep working after the singer left. Four hands sit beside the Grove Tender: the Seal Loom, the Tide Pump, the Wind Snare and the Ward Drum.\n\nHow:\n1. Raise Pulse within 8 \u2014 a Drumheart, Resonator or Ley Collector.\n2. Place the hand. Each one drinks Pulse only when it actually works.\n3. A held redstone stills it. A comparator reads what it is doing.\n4. Rank it in Echo Attune, Bind, then Manifest. Ranked hands beat faster. Pulse per move stays the same, so the lattice feels the extra speed.\n5. Open the next pages for each hand, then the walkthroughs.",
            "SEAL LOOM\n\nA recipe is a polite request. The Seal Loom writes it onto a Recipe Seal and weaves it forever.\n\nHow:\n1. Craft a Recipe Seal from a Blank Seal and paper.\n2. Place the Seal Loom. Hopper ingredients into the three-by-three from the sides or top.\n3. Seat the blank seal in the middle slot. Arrange the recipe in the grid.\n4. Sneak-use the loom empty-handed. The seal remembers that recipe.\n5. Keep matching ingredients in the grid. Every second it spends 6 Pulse and weaves one result. Rank shortens that second; Pulse per craft stays 6.",
            "TIDE PUMP\n\nWater goes where it is asked. The Tide Pump asks both ways.\n\nHow:\n1. Place tanks on both faces \u2014 Spirit Cisterns, or any fluid handler.\n2. The arrow face is the front. By default it draws from the front and pushes into the back.\n3. Sneak-use to reverse: now it pushes into the front.\n4. Each second it moves 250 mB for 4 Pulse. Rank shortens that second; Pulse per 250 mB stays 4.\n5. Click empty-handed to read the current direction. A lever pauses it.",
            "WIND SNARE\n\nDropped things remember the wind. The Wind Snare calls them home.\n\nHow:\n1. Place it near a farm, a shatter station, or anywhere items fall.\n2. Keep 2 Pulse nearby per stack it catches, up to eight stacks a second, within 8 blocks.\n3. Rank shortens that second. Pulse per stack stays 2.\n4. Open it like a chest, or hopper the catch out of any face.\n5. A lever pauses both the catch and the hoppers. It does not steal from other inventories.",
            "WARD DRUM\n\nA drum can keep the dark at the edge of camp.\n\nHow:\n1. Place it where hostiles walk. It listens in an 8-block sphere.\n2. Keep 8 Pulse nearby. Each second it strikes one Enemy for 4 magic and a shove. Rank shortens that second; Pulse per strike stays 8.\n3. Players are never the target.\n4. A lever silences it. A comparator reads 15 on a hit, 0 while it waits.\n5. It is a watch, not a farm. Pair a Wake Bell if the deaths should pay Pulse back.",
            "SONG THREAD\n\nRedstone is a shout. Song Thread is a hummed line through the air.\n\nHow:\n1. Craft Song Thread from redstone and Loom Thread.\n2. Place it. It carries 0 to 15 in all six directions and decays by one per block.\n3. Vanilla dust, levers, plates, Song Vines and comparators all speak to it.\n4. Snap song plates onto faces along the line.\n\nA wall of thread is a wall of song. Keep the line short if you need a full 15 at the far end. For a tendril that hugs stone, see Song Vine.",
            "SONG VINE\n\nA Pattern-weaver's song follows the stone. Song Vine is a tendril that crawls every face of a block.\n\nHow:\n1. Craft eight vines from one Song Thread and a Spirit Reed.\n2. Click a solid face. The vine sits in the air cell on that face.\n3. Click an existing vine with another vine to add a second face on the same cell \u2014 floor and wall, or every side of a cube.\n4. Power decays by one per step, including around corners onto a neighbouring face.\n5. It speaks to Song Thread, song plates, vanilla dust and comparators.\n\nBreak the block to pick up one vine per face. Relays still carry items; vines carry only the song.",
            "VERSE CALL AND ANSWER\n\nSixteen verses. Two plates singing the same verse hear each other without a vine.\n\nHow:\n1. Snap a Verse Call onto a face. It reads redstone from every side except its facing.\n2. Snap a Verse Answer onto a face within 32 blocks, same world. It sings out of its facing.\n3. Sneak-use either plate to cycle verse 1 to 16. Click empty-handed to read the verse and the strength.\n4. Several Calls of one verse: the Answer takes the loudest.\n5. A mismatched verse stays silent. Relays still move items; these plates move only redstone.\n\nAir Seal in the Call, Bone Chime in the Answer. Pattern-weavers favour clocks and Storm Wing.",
            "SONG PLATES\n\nThirteen plates. Each does one job. The facing is the output.\n\nHow:\n1. Snap a plate onto a solid face, the same way you snap a relay.\n2. Binary plates (Chorus, Gathering, Discord, Hush) read left and right of the facing.\n3. Unary plates (Inverse, Echo, Drift, Strike, Chance, Tally, Verse) read the back.\n4. Memory reads left to set and right to clear.\n5. Heartbeat needs no input. Sneak-use Heartbeat, Drift or Tally to change the count.\n\nThe next pages name each plate. Pattern-weavers favour redstone, clocks and Storm Wing.",
            "CHORUS, GATHERING, DISCORD, HUSH\n\nFour ways two voices can agree.\n\nHow:\n1. Chorus (AND) sings only when left and right are both live.\n2. Gathering (OR) sings when either side is live.\n3. Discord (XOR) sings when the sides disagree.\n4. Hush (NAND) sings unless both sides are live.\n\nOutput is 15 or 0 from the facing. Place Song Thread on that face to carry the answer.",
            "INVERSE AND ECHO\n\nOne voice, turned or carried.\n\nHow:\n1. Inverse (NOT) sings while the back is quiet, and hushes when the back is live.\n2. Echo (BUFFER) copies the back: live stays live.\n\nUse Inverse to turn a Pulse Threshold into a 'too empty' alarm. Use Echo to strengthen a fading Song Thread.",
            "MEMORY, TALLY, VERSE\n\nThe plates that remember.\n\nHow:\n1. Memory: a live left sets it; a live right clears it. Output stays until told otherwise.\n2. Tally: each rising edge on the back adds one. Output 15 once the count meets the threshold. Sneak-use to cycle the threshold 1 to 8. A rising left resets the count.\n3. Verse: each rising edge on the back steps 1, 2, 3, 4 and emits 4, 8, 12, 15. A comparator reads the same number.\n\nA rite-on-a-clock loop is Memory plus Heartbeat plus a Rite Pedestal comparator.",
            "HEARTBEAT, DRIFT, STRIKE, CHANCE\n\nTime, delay, a tap, a coin.\n\nHow:\n1. Heartbeat pulses 15 for one tick, then rests. Sneak-use cycles 20, 40, 80, 160 ticks.\n2. Drift copies the back, but only after it has stayed live for 4, 8, 16 or 32 ticks (sneak-use to cycle).\n3. Strike emits one tick of 15 on a rising back, then goes quiet. The Drumheart's struck-signal language.\n4. Chance flips a coin on each rising back: 15 or 0 until the back falls.\n\nA one-second Heartbeat on a Drumheart is a 24-Pulse beat if the edge lands in tempo.",
            "WALKTHROUGH: TEND A GROVE\n\n1. Craft the Grove Tender (Earth Seal, hoe, copper, Bound Echo, planks).\n2. Till a 9-by-9 of farmland (or dirt for saplings, sand for cactus). Place the tender in the middle at crop height.\n3. Put a Drumheart or Resonator within 8. Hopper wheat seeds into the top.\n4. Wait. It plants for 4 Pulse, then harvests and replants ripe wheat for 12, keeping one seed.\n5. For trees: hopper saplings. It plants, urges growth for 16 Pulse, then takes logs and leaves above.\n6. For cane: hopper sugar cane onto sand or dirt beside water. It cuts the top of a three-high stalk.\nWhat you now have: a bed that plants, grows and harvests without you standing there.\nNext: a Wind Snare beside it to catch anything that still drops, and a Seal Loom for the harvest.",
            "WALKTHROUGH: IMPRINT A SEAL\n\n1. Craft a Seal Loom and a Recipe Seal (Blank Seal and paper).\n2. Place the loom. Put the blank seal in the middle slot.\n3. Arrange sticks in the grid the way you would craft them on a table.\n4. Sneak-use the loom empty-handed. The seal tooltip names the recipe.\n5. Hopper sticks in the top or sides. Keep 6 Pulse within 8. Take sticks-of-result from below \u2014 or hoppers will.\n6. Swap the seal for another imprinted seal when you want a different recipe. A lever pauses the weave.\nWhat you now have: one reusable Recipe Seal and a loom that crafts while you walk away.\nNext: Song Thread and a Heartbeat plate if you want the loom paused on a clock.",
            "WALKTHROUGH: A SONG CLOCK\n\n1. Place a Drumheart. Point a Pulse Gauge at it so you can see charge as redstone.\n2. Place a Heartbeat plate on a solid face nearby. Sneak-use until it reads 20 ticks \u2014 one second.\n3. Run Song Thread from the Heartbeat's facing to the Drumheart. A one-second rising edge is a 24-Pulse beat.\n4. Optional: a Pulse Threshold on the Drumheart at 75 percent, Inverse plate on that line, to pause a hungry machine when Pulse runs low.\n5. Optional: Memory plate set by a lever, cleared by the Inverse, so a whole wing of the camp stills together.\nWhat you now have: a clock that speaks the drum's language, and the plates to hush it.\nNext: Chorus plates to require two conditions, and the Ward Drum if the clock is for a farm that should not run while you sleep in camp.",
            "DAWN STAG\n\nA dawn grazer that carries the old forest song in its antlers. Breed with wheat; brush adults for Dawn Velvet. Bond an adult with a Bonding Charm to ride it without a saddle.",
            "LANTERN FOX\n\nA shy dusk forager whose tail marks safe paths. Breed with sweet berries; brush adults for Lantern Down. Bond an adult with a Bonding Charm for a lantern that follows you.",
            "MOSSBACK\n\nA patient wetland gardener with a living shell. Breed with seagrass; brush adults for a naturally shed Mossback Scale. Bond an adult with a Bonding Charm for a walking saddlebag.",
            "ASHBOUND\n\nThe remains of a broken fire rite. Its melee strikes briefly ignite; keep water close.",
            "ROOTBOUND\n\nA grove guardian twisted by a severed ley line. Slow but sturdy; its blows root travellers briefly.",
            "REED STALKER\n\nA marsh hunter concealed among spirit reeds. Fast strikes carry a short poison.",
            "SHARDBACK\n\nA crystal-field scavenger armored in singing stone. Keep your distance from its heavy shove.",
            "HOLLOW SENTINEL\n\nAn empty watchman that still guards the ancient roads. Its touch weakens the grip of attackers.",
            "STORM MOTH\n\nA storm-fed spirit with vast veil wings. A bright gathering of motes warns of its gust; cover breaks the attack.",
            "CINDER IMP\n\nA nimble ember spirit. It gathers sparks before a burning bolt; the spell never ignites terrain.",
            "MOURNING BELL\n\nA floating relic that remembers the lost tribes. Its telegraphed chime slows; shelter interrupts the song.",
            "RIFT HOUND\n\nA hunter drawn to tears in the lattice. It closes distance quickly but cannot cross worlds by itself.",
            "ECHO WEAVER\n\nAn eight-legged keeper of broken songs. Its bite slows prey without placing webs or damaging the camp."
        );
    }
}
